# The first window's field played with the keyboard alone, so DOSBox's AUTOTYPE can play it: typing, Backspace and typing again. The steps before the first frame are the first window's set-up, which a live session performs itself; the first frame is its first mark.
desk-scenario 1
screen 640 480
depths 8 4
open notes 60 60 300 180 "Notes"
label notes 12 12 "The first window."
open welcome 220 150 340 200 "Welcome to Desk"
label welcome 12 12 "Type something:"
field welcome 12 36 300
pointer 320 240
frame start
# Typing goes to Welcome's field.
type "desk"
frame typed
# Backspace twice removes "sk".
key Backspace down
key Backspace up
key Backspace down
key Backspace up
frame erased
# Typing again.
type "ok"
frame again
